From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P90 native Linux port <local>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 18:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: intel_scu: leave watchdog stopped for kexec

The Lenovo P90/Moorefield production kernel re-arms the Intel SCU watchdog
from the reboot notifier.  That is appropriate for ordinary restart, halt and
poweroff paths, but it is hostile to kexec: userspace can stop the watchdog
before calling kexec, then kernel_restart_prepare() invokes this notifier and
starts the watchdog again immediately before machine_kexec().

This patch is for rebuilt test kernels only.  It keeps ordinary reboot and
poweroff behavior intact by default, while allowing the kexec path to preserve
the already-stopped watchdog state when the command string is "kexec reboot".
Upstream kernels pass this command string through kernel_restart_prepare().
Lenovo's stock 3.10 tree often passes NULL, so this patch mainly protects
second-stage/rebuilt kernels and documents the intended handoff behavior.

---
 drivers/watchdog/intel_scu_watchdog_evo.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/intel_scu_watchdog_evo.c b/drivers/watchdog/intel_scu_watchdog_evo.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/intel_scu_watchdog_evo.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/intel_scu_watchdog_evo.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/kernel_stat.h>
 #include <linux/rpmsg.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include <linux/nmi.h>
 #include <asm/intel_scu_ipcutil.h>
 #include <asm/intel_mid_rpmsg.h>
@@ -503,6 +503,7 @@ static int reboot_notifier(struct notifier_block *this,
 			   unsigned long code,
 			   void *another_unused)
 {
+	const char *cmd = another_unused;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (code == SYS_RESTART || code == SYS_HALT || code == SYS_POWER_OFF) {
@@ -510,6 +511,16 @@ static int reboot_notifier(struct notifier_block *this,
 		pr_warn("Reboot notifier\n");
 
+		/*
+		 * kexec is not a firmware-mediated reboot.  If userspace has
+		 * explicitly stopped the SCU watchdog before entering kexec,
+		 * do not arm it again immediately before machine_kexec().
+		 */
+		if (code == SYS_RESTART && cmd && !strcmp(cmd, "kexec reboot")) {
+			pr_warn("leaving watchdog state unchanged for kexec\n");
+			return NOTIFY_DONE;
+		}
+
 		if (watchdog_set_appropriate_timeouts())
 			pr_crit("reboot notifier cant set time\n");
 
 		switch (code) {
-- 
2.0.0
